<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Grand Principality of Ryazan</h1><p class="st-meta">1129 CE – 1521 CE (approx.) · capital Ryazan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A frontier principality on the Oka, first to fall to the Mongols in 1237 and the last major Russian land absorbed by Moscow.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a> on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oka-river">Oka</a> belonged to the Chernigov dynasty and was ruled together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murom">Murom</a>. Around 1129 the two lands separated, and Ryazan became a principality of its own under descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-sviatoslavich">Yaroslav Sviatoslavich</a>, bordering the steppe and the forest lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mordvins">Mordvins</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its princes were frequently at war with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vladimir-suzdal">Vladimir-Suzdal</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a>, while facing steppe raids from the south. In December 1237 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed the old city and killed Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-igorevich-of-ryazan">Yuri Igorevich</a>, an event later told in the tale of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evpaty-kolovrat">Evpaty Kolovrat</a>. The capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Pereyaslavl-Ryazansky</a>, the modern city of Ryazan.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oleg-ii-of-ryazan">Oleg Ivanovich</a>, who ruled for most of 1350 to 1402, stood up to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-donskoy">Dmitry Donskoy</a> and kept out of the Battle of Kulikovo. Afterwards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow's</a> influence grew steadily, and in 1521 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-iii-of-moscow">Vasily III</a> arrested <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-ivanovich-of-ryazan">Ivan Ivanovich</a>, the last grand prince, and annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/grand-principality-of-ryazan.jpg" alt="Grand Principality of Ryazan" width="320" height="185"><figcaption>Image: Hellerick · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Principality_of_Ryazan_14th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1129 CE – 1521 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ryazan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yuri Igorevich, Oleg Ivanovich, Ivan Ivanovich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old East Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Principality of Ryazan, Ryazan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1325&amp;focus=grand-principality-of-ryazan" aria-label="Grand Principality of Ryazan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5555 307 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Grand Principality of Ryazan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5875 563L5724 651M5875 563L7559 780M5875 563L6352 637M5875 563L5820 533M5875 563L5876 577"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5724 651h0M7559 780h0M6352 637h0M5820 533h0M5876 577h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5875 563h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5875 563h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ryazan. <a href="/atlas?year=1325&amp;focus=grand-principality-of-ryazan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
